  "caption": "The moon boot came off and Quinn planned a victory lap. It turned into a victory limp, plus one suspiciously small calf.\n\nWeeks of immobilisation can weaken the calf, stiffen the ankle and dull your balance, and some evening swelling is often normal for a while.\n\nWhat often helps: ankle circles and knee-to-wall bends, calf raises progressing from two feet to one, practising normal heel-to-toe walking, then balance work and gradual hops and jogs. Elevation and compression socks may help evening swelling. Always follow your doctor's clearance timeline.\n\nPain or swelling that gets worse week on week, numbness, tingling or a skin concern are worth checking with your doctor.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
